# upstream-routing drives audit-upstream-routing.sh (and copies of it with core-paths.sh beside them), the core guard hook,
# and reads the manifest and setup-sites data the guard and the glob set come from. Every other file is built under mktemp.
# core/scripts/ is NOT declared whole: nothing enumerates it. The subject reads core-paths.sh from its own directory by name,
# and the fixture copies exactly those two, so both are declared one by one, against a fresh sandbox read-set trace.
# core/hooks/ is declared as the guard and the one file it sources as a same-directory sibling (ai-dlc-core-guard.sh,
# ai-dlc-context-provenance.sh).
# The four resolved inputs are REQUIRED and printed where the fixture resolves them.
!core/scripts/audit-upstream-routing.sh
!core/hooks/ai-dlc-core-guard.sh
!core/skills/ai-dlc/core-manifest.md
!core/skills/ai-dlc-update/reconcile/setup-sites.md
core/scripts/core-paths.sh
core/hooks/ai-dlc-context-provenance.sh
core/fixtures/lib/report.sh
core/fixtures/lib/mutant.sh
